# Wave W17-P (Route 118): ford turf — river-bank turf: a rich bank green with wet-edge dark flecks where the river’s breath keeps the sward damp and a whisper of pale foam fleck along the water side (design: calm speckled grass along a proud old river crossing; the shipped ford planks stand byte-preserved by spec at the crossing itself). Route 118’s own ground — wetter than Route 117’s dry field green and split from Route 119’s rain-soaked gauge turf by degree: this bank is river-damp, not sky-drowned.
